PKI store for cyclic issuer / chain depth limit tests (check_pki.c, suite `chain depth`).

Tests load the store via `SOPC_PKIProvider_CreateFromStore("./cycle_pki_test")`
with revocation checks disabled.

## Test cases

| Test | Leaf validated | Chain (leaf to issuers) | Expected |
|------|----------------|-------------------------|----------|
| `cycle_pki_mutual_ca_rejected` | `leaf_cycle.der` | leaf -> `ca_cycle_a` -> `ca_cycle_b` -> `ca_cycle_a` -> ... (mutual cross-sign, no path to a trusted root) | NOK, Untrusted |

CA A and B cross-sign each other (`ca_cycle_a` names B as issuer and is signed by B; same for B).
Neither is in the trusted store. `decoy_root.der` is unrelated: it only allows
`CreateFromStore` to succeed. Chain building must stop at the intermediate depth cap
instead of looping forever.

Run (from `build/bin` after POST_BUILD copy):

```bash
CK_FORK=no CK_RUN_SUITE="PKI API test" CK_RUN_CASE="chain depth" ./check_helpers
```

## Fixture files

| File | Role |
|------|------|
| issuers/certs/ca_cycle_a.der | CA A, issuer B, signed by B |
| issuers/certs/ca_cycle_b.der | CA B, issuer A, signed by A |
| trusted/certs/decoy_root.der | Unrelated trusted root (PKI store bootstrap only) |
| leaf_cycle.der | End entity, issuer A, signed by A |

Regeneration (requires Python 3 and the `cryptography` package):

```bash
cd tests/ClientServer/data/cert/cycle_pki_test
python3 generate_certs.py
```
